o adds holding cost every day it sits in stock.\n- **Product 1, candidate 0 vs 5.** Candidate 0 loses about 62 sales and is left with about 22 unsold units. Candidate 5 loses about 12 sales but ends with about 91 unsold. At 12 per lost sale and 9 per unsold unit, both come to about 950. Candidate 5 then pays about 340 more in holding.\n- **Product 0.** Candidate 5 loses about 170 less on lost sales and unsold stock. It pays about 270 more in holding, so overall it is roughly even with candidate 0 or slightly worse.\n- **Warehouse capacity on day 15.** Product 1's spike (93 forecast) arrives that day. Candidate 5 is carrying more stock, so space runs out and about 20 of its 130 units are lost. Candidate 0's 118 units fit.\n- **Effect of random demand.** If demand runs high, candidate 0 loses more sales. If it runs low, the larger plans lose more to write-offs, holding and capacity overflow. On expected profit, candidate 0 stays ahead."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3788, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3788}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T07:40:03.994Z", "request_id": "req_011CgBDJpYUjk4hvYkxrNPE1"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01GymjMBppZ4j7LitAMzGwHg", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgBDJpynE7smvuevgnfNQ", "type": "message", "